  "worked_solution": "According to Newton\u2019s second law\n\n$$\nF=ma,\n$$\n\n \nwhere $F$ is the force, $m$ is the mass, and $a$ is the acceleration.\n\nTo find the velocity $v(t),$ we differentiate the displacement $s(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t+{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t+2t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the acceleration $a(t),$ we differentiate the velocity $v(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}\u2061t+2t) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t+2 \\\\  & =2-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the force in Newtons, is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F & =ma \\\\  & =4\\cdot (2-\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t) \\\\  & =8-4\\operatorname{sin}\u2061t.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
